  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nDry weather is expected through at least early Saturday as high\npressure moves east across the region. Rising 500 mb heights\nunder shortwave ridging should result in high temperatures near\nto above seasonable levels today. A digging shortwave trough is\nexpected to begin to advance out of the Midwest tonight into\nSaturday. Expect an increase in mid and high level clouds\ntonight through Saturday morning in advance of the trough. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nThe shortwave trough is expected to continue to deepen as it\ntracks toward the Upper Ohio Valley region late Saturday and\nSunday. At the same time, an associated surface low is progged \nto track NE across the Upper Ohio Valley/eastern Great Lakes\nregion. Increasing moisture and ascent with an initial lead\nshortwave should return shower and thunderstorm chances Saturday\nafternoon across Ohio, overspreading the remainder of the area\nSaturday night. \n\nPeriods of showers and scattered thunderstorms are expected on\nSunday as the main trough axis approaches, and the surface low\ntracks across the region. Clouds could limit instability, with\nML CAPE currently progged at 1000 j/kg or less. Machine learning\nalso keeps chances for severe storms low, though shear is\nexpected to increase with increasing flow aloft. Locally heavy\nrain will also be possible as PWATs approach 1.8 inches, though\nsome indication of a dry slot Sunday afternoon ahead of the \nsurface low would limit this potential. The surface cold front \nis currently expected to cross the area late Sunday/Sunday \nnight.\n\nModel ensembles then indicate a persistent trough across the\nEastern Great Lakes and Ohio Valley region early in the week.\nThis trough should weaken some through the week, though\nsignificant uncertainty exists in exact placement and strength.\nOverall, expect daily, diurnally driven shower and thunderstorm\nchances under this pattern.",
